# 2026-11-21 the Qwen3.8-27B file published in litert-community/Qwen3.8-27B (Qwen3.8-27B_wi4b32_32k.litertlm, Hub
# commit 392f105a of 2026-11-20 22:53 UTC) on the Mac Studio (M4 Max) GPU: dashboard-job sittings whose payload is
# the platform's session anchor row alone (matrices/anchors.cells, byte-identical: the job re-judges the payload by the
# anchor records in its own campaign), each followed, inside the same Mac measurement window, by the file's protocol
# launches. They cannot be a row here: the Mac runner (scripts/bench_matrix_mac.sh) runs the yardstick, whose LiteRT-LM
# is the vendored release (v0.19.0), and the file's metadata asks for LiteRT-LM 0.20.0 (min_runtime_version), so the
# launches run a LiteRT-LM main build as its CLI:
#   build = litert_lm_advanced_main built for macos_arm64 at LiteRT-LM main 5dcf0602 (2026-11-20; the commit of the
#           Android side build main-5dcf06020 in android/engine-pins.json) as the checkout builds it (bazel 7.6.1,
#           -c opt, no source change): on macOS its GPU path is the ML Drift WebGPU accelerator compiled from source
#           and linked in (log: "Statically linked GPU accelerator registered."), with the commit's prebuilt
#           libGemmaModelConstraintProvider.dylib and libwebgpu_dawn.dylib beside it; the binary's sha256, otool -L and
#           build info go into the campaign dir; the records stamp engineVersion main-5dcf06020;
#   file  = Qwen3.8-27B_wi4b32_32k.litertlm (15,169,077,248 B, LFS sha256 94867fc2...99ded6) on the Mac's internal
#           disk; the CLI writes its GPU caches beside the model (a program cache and a weight cache), and one launch
#           before the first window built them, so every launch in a window reads them;
#   rows  = the Android command form (android/bench/run_cell.py engine_command): --backend=gpu --benchmark
#           --benchmark_prefill_tokens=1024 --benchmark_decode_tokens=256 --async=false --max_num_tokens=2048, one
#           process per launch, 300 s between launches, a 5-s sampler of the other processes' CPU per launch (ps %cpu
#           above 30 % outside the launch's process tree; kernel_task and WindowServer apart, as sys=) and one retake of
#           a launch another process overlapped (a launch overlapped twice is no number);
#   id    = litert-community/Qwen3.8-27B/wi4b32_32k (ios/BenchmarkApp/Sources/Models/ModelCatalog.swift).
# Sitting 1 (campaign 2026-11-21-dashboard-v1-m4max-qwen38-27b-mac, 4 launches planned) holds no number: all five of
# its tries were overlapped (cmux alone in four, NotificationCenter in one).
# Sittings 2 and 3 (suffixes qwen38-27b-s2 and qwen38-27b-s3), decided before sitting 2's window: the sampler reads
# cmux (a terminal app on the Mac's screen) as it reads WindowServer (sys=, never an overlap), and every sample line
# also records cmux's %cpu; NotificationCenter, Chrome, rclone and every other process still overlap. Each plans 3
# launches, the runs of a protocol row on the Android route (android/bench/run_campaign.py: a cell's runs default to
# 3), and starts a launch only when the window still holds it and its retake.
# Sitting 2 holds no number: Docker Desktop's CLI plugin, already running when its window opened, overlapped both tries
# of its first launch at 70-84 % CPU. Sitting 3's window opens only after 60 s of the sampler's readings outside it
# (every 5 s) show no process above 30 % other than those it reads as sys= (kernel_task, WindowServer and cmux), and no
# Docker VM runs.
# The first launch in each of sitting 1's and sitting 2's windows ran at prefill 176.6 and 176.1 tok/s, and so did one
# launch outside the windows (176.6), while the six other launches ran at 205.9-206.4. The cause is not known: a first
# launch stays in the row as measured, and sitting 3's NOTES give the row's prefill spread.
# The consoles become schema-v1 records in the payload dir's app-path-cli/ (scripts/import_litert_cli.py: the Android
# route's parsers; the arm, the KV allocation's target_number and the overlap verdict per launch), with the console,
# the sampler's lines and the manifest in its cli/ dir.
# Estimate for sitting 3: one Mac window of about 13 min (the job about 1 min, the launches about 12 min), 24 min with
# two retakes.
# The jobs run inside the window through a local wrapper, with these arguments (sittings 2 and 3: --suffix
# qwen38-27b-s2, qwen38-27b-s3):
#   python3 scripts/dashboard_job.py m4max --cells matrices/qwen38-27b-main-mac.cells --suffix qwen38-27b --once --no-page-commit --no-post

